snapshot-from=router-for-me/models main on 2026-09-29: adds gpt-6.1-sol (codex-team/plus/pro and the Codex client catalog; free-plan accounts do not receive it, verified against chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex/models with a free token), refreshes Codex client priorities/descriptions/plans, and takes upstream's claude-sonnet-5-5 row in place of the fork's hand-made one. Fork adjustment on top of the remote models.json: gpt-6.1-sol version is "gpt-6.1" (remote copy-pastes "gpt-6.0"). thinking.levels stay low..max even though the Codex client catalog lists "ultra": the backend rejects reasoning.effort=ultra on the wire ("Supported values are: none, minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, and max", checked 2026-09-29), so ultra is a Codex CLI client-side mode and the proxy clamps it to max with a warning. The Codex client catalog is the remote file verbatim. Fork adjustment 2026-10-07: adds claude-haiku-5-5 to the claude section (released 2026-10-07 with Claude Code 2.1.293, which made it the default Haiku; 1M context, 128k output, adaptive thinking with effort low..max and a medium default, same tokenizer as 4.7+; cloned from the claude-sonnet-5-5 row because router-for-me/models main had no row for it as of its 2026-10-04 commit). Fork adjustment 2026-10-21 (v8.0.38 rebase): the thinking objects of claude-opus-4-7, claude-opus-4-8, claude-fable-5, claude-fable-5-1, claude-opus-5-5 and claude-sonnet-5-5 are taken from upstream v8.0.38's embedded models.json (ad9e456d, upstream issue 6698): sonnet-5-5 rejects thinking.type "disabled" and needs "between_tools"; opus-5-5, fable-5 and fable-5-1 cannot switch thinking off (zero_allowed false), so a request to disable it becomes low-effort adaptive, the none-to-lowest conversion the no-substitution design keeps; the adaptive models lose the budget min/max. Fork adjustment 2026-10-26 (v8.0.44 rebase): devin_models.json is upstream v8.0.44's embedded file verbatim (3dae075d folds the swe-2 lightning UIDs into one swe-2-lightning row; the registry code that reads it changed in the same commit). Every other row, the antigravity section (no claude-opus-5-5-high / claude-sonnet-5-5-high rows) and the Codex client catalog stay as reviewed on 2026-10-07. Snapshot 2026-11-04 (v8.0.54 rebase): models.json and codex_client_models.json are upstream v8.0.54's embedded files, read in docs/fork/audits/v8.0.54.md, because the registry code that reads them changed in the range (19398539 Codex client template and restrictions, b63322b9 Antigravity Claude 5.5 thinkingLevel) and upstream's tests depend on the new rows. Upstream now ships claude-haiku-5-5 and the antigravity claude-opus-5-5-high / claude-sonnet-5-5-high rows, so the fork's hand-made haiku row and its antigravity exclusion are retired; it adds gpt-6.1-terra, gemini-4-argon, kimi-k3.1-pro, muse-wonder and grok imagine rows and drops gpt-5.5 from the Codex tiers (no gpt-5.5 traffic in main.log on 2026-11-04). The one fork adjustment kept: gpt-6.1-sol version is "gpt-6.1" in codex-team/plus/pro (upstream still "gpt-6.0"). devin_models.json is unchanged. Snapshot 2026-11-09 (v8.0.62 rebase): models.json and devin_models.json are upstream v8.0.62's embedded files, read in docs/fork/audits/v8.0.62.md (adds gpt-6-chat-thinking, devin swe-2-flash, nemotron-3-5-super and gpt-6-1-terra rows); the gpt-6.1-sol version fix is kept; codex_client_models.json is unchanged in the range. Fork adjustment 2026-11-09: adds claude-fable-5-2 to the claude section, cloned from claude-fable-5-1 because upstream v8.0.62 and upstream main have no row. Measured through a side instance on a pool OAuth account on 2026-11-09: Anthropic serves it (response model claude-fable-5-2, bare and as claude-fable-5-2[1m] from Claude Code 2.1.319); context 1000000 from the error 'prompt is too long: 2200064 tokens > 1000000 maximum'; max_completion_tokens 128000 from 'max_tokens: 1000000 > 128000, which is the maximum allowed number of output tokens for claude-fable-5-2'; effort low, medium, high, xhigh and max each answered 200. Not measured, carried from the 5.1 row: zero_allowed false, dynamic_allowed true, image input. created is the day it was first observed, not a release date. Anthropic refuses it to a client below Claude Code 2.1.290 ('Claude Code 2.1.280 does not support this model; version 2.1.290 or newer is required'), so cloaked requests need claude-header-defaults.user-agent at 2.1.290 or later.
